## 🛠️ Database Schema Context (Prisma)
Understanding these structures is essential for binding fields:
- **`Team` Model**:
  - `id` (String, primary key)
  - `name` (String)
  - `groupCode` (String, e.g., `"A#100161"`)
  - `domain` (String, domain area)
  - `ranking` (One-to-one relation with `GroupRanking` model containing `rank` [Int] and `totalPoints` [Int])
  - `members` (Array of `User` models)
  - `projects` (Array of `Project` models containing `id`, `name`, `description`, `status`)
  - `achievements` (Array of `AdminAchievement` models containing `title`, `description`, `points`, `date`)
- **`User` Model** (where `role` == `'STUDENT'`):
  - `id`, `fullName`, `email`, `regNo`
  - `year` (academic year), `department` (dept name), `deptCode` (abbreviation)
  - `gender` (M/F), `resident` (H/D for Hosteller/Day-scholar)
  - `ssgDomain` (Hardware/Software)
  - `rewardPoints` (Int), `activityPoints` (Int)
  - `team` (Relation to `Team` model)
  - `userSkills` (Array of `UserSkill` models containing `skillName`, `skillType`, `totalPoints`, `skillRank`, `totalRanks`)

